course: dictionary
lesson: 11411
title: Things that build up over time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To accumulate means to collect more and more of something over time, or to grow bigger slowly as things build up. «Sam's savings accumulated each week, because he added a little money every Friday.» The pile grew bit by bit, so accumulate means to gather more and more over time.
explain: Dust is a good example from science. «Dust accumulates on the shelf if nobody cleans it for a month.» Nobody drops a big heap there all at once. The dust builds up slowly, and accumulate is the word for that slow build-up.
explain: Games work the same way. «Maya's points accumulated quickly as she answered the questions.» Ask yourself: is something being gathered and growing over time? If yes, accumulate probably fits. Check by swapping in "built up" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accumulate means to collect or gather more and more of something over time.
fact: Accumulate can also mean to grow larger by building up slowly.
fact: The other forms are accumulates, accumulated and accumulating.
fact: «Snow began to accumulate on the hills» means the snow built up layer by layer.
fact: In geography, sediment accumulates over a very long time and can form rock.
exercise: «Maya's points accumulated during the quiz.» What does accumulated mean? | *Gathered up bit by bit over time | Written on a card | Lost all at once | Shared with a friend
exercise: «Dust accumulates on the shelf if nobody cleans it.» Which word means the same as accumulates? | *Builds up | Vanishes | Blows away | Shines
exercise: «Snow began to accumulate on the hills by noon.» Find and copy the word that shows the snow building up. | hills | noon | began | *accumulate
test: «Savings accumulate when you add money each week.» What does accumulate mean here? | To count backwards | *To build up over time | To spend quickly | To shrink and disappear
test: Miss Lee says, «The dust will accumulate if we do not clean.» What is she warning about? | Dust will be blown away by the wind | The room will be made clean at once | *Dust will build up slowly over time | Dust will change colour
exam: Which phrase means building up wealth slowly over time? | *Accumulate wealth | Shout loudly | Lose a ball | Run out of time
